# Guardrails

## Do not break the stream path

When editing UI (`app/page.tsx`, `components/*`), preserve:
- POST `/api/build` + `fetch().body.getReader()` frame parsing (`data: ` prefix, `\n\n` delimiter)
- `handleEvent` switch on `BuildEvent.type`
- `runningRef` one-build-at-a-time guard

Visual-only changes belong in components; do not move agent logic into the client.

## Do not pull server code into the client bundle

Never import `lib/cursor.ts`, `lib/scratch.ts`, or `@cursor/sdk` from `"use client"` files. Shared types/constants: `lib/events.ts` only.

## Keep the agent-built app simple

The demo app the agent creates must stay **vanilla HTML/CSS/JS** (three files, no bundler, no `npm install`, no fetch). Changes to scope belong in `lib/prompts.ts`, not ad-hoc prompt strings in routes or components.

## No browser persistence

No `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, or IndexedDB — each run is stateless server-side. Transcript lives in React state; proof lives on disk in scratch dir.

## Do not move scratch workspace into the repo

Agent output stays in `{tmpdir}/say-so/`. Moving it under the project root will reload the dev server when the agent writes files.

## Cut order when behind

Drop from the bottom: live VM stream → cloud agent → voice (text fallback always wired) → proof polish. Never let flex work break the floor stream.

## Next.js version

This is Next.js 16.2.7 — read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before changing routing, route handlers, or config. See `AGENTS.md` for the project entry point.
